# State Management

## Global (Zustand)

- Use for cross-component or persisted UI state only.
- Location: `src/modules/{feature}/store/` or `src/core/store/`.
- Typed stores; flat shape; use `set()` — never mutate directly.
- Middleware (`persist`, `devtools`) only where needed per slice.
- Do not store server-fetched entities in Zustand.

## Forms (React Hook Form + Zod)

- `useForm`, `useFormContext`, `useFieldArray` for inputs.
- Schemas in `schemas/`; `zodResolver`; form logic in `hooks/`.
- Prefer `control`, `watch`, `setValue` over ad-hoc local state.
- Keep form state separate from Zustand and unrelated React state.

## URL state (`nuqs`)

- Use `useQueryState()` for filters, tabs, pagination synced to the URL.
- Do not manually sync URL and local/global state.

## Server state (TanStack Query)

- All server data via React Query in custom `hooks/`.
- Invalidate/refetch after Server Actions or Zustand-driven events.
- Minimize client state; prefer RSC and server fetching where possible.

## Defaults

- Local state first; lift only when shared across routes or features.
- Avoid deep nesting in stores; use semantic slices.
